# BEAVIS2 lab host hard rules

These rules bind the **BEAVIS2** Windows lab (`192.168.55.197`) used for embedded-live
Playwright, password recovery, and HSM/crypto custody tests.

## Credential identities (never drift)

| Rule | Detail |
| --- | --- |
| **Rotation test accounts** | **`liebsoft`** and **`lanicu`** only — sourced from the HKLM snapshot in `pim-offline-server/src/bin/seed_dev/lab_fixtures.rs` and restored by `cargo run --bin seed-dev -- --confirm --dev-fixtures [--reset]`. |
| **Forbidden rotation target** | Never run password rotation, group membership changes, or `--force` rotate against **`phil`** or any operator account outside the two lab identities above. |
| **Endpoint discovery** | Tests MUST resolve the BEAVIS2 row via `discoverBeavis2DualEndpoint()` (machine name contains `beavis2`, carries both identities). Do not hardcode stale sync names like `BEAVIS2-DUAL-20260602023604`. |
| **Canonical machine_id** | `3a7b240e-9327-44b8-97b6-38fb7812b3b2` after seed-dev; `machine_name` is `Beavis2`. |

## SoftHSM (required for HSM / crypto tests)

| Rule | Detail |
| --- | --- |
| **Token** | SoftHSM2 at `C:\SoftHSM2\lib\softhsm2-x64.dll` (or `softhsm2.dll` fallback). |
| **Lab user PIN** | **`2222`** on preferred slots (`1668200181`, `1075368336`, `200080059`); try **`1111`** as fallback in helpers. |
| **DB connection row** | After every `db-init --confirm`, run `scripts/Fix-LabSoftHsmLibraryPath.ps1` to insert **Local SoftHSM** (+ **Local SoftHSM Mirror** for Set Default e2e). |
| **UI PIN fields** | When a sealed PIN is stored, the Keys tab shows **User PIN (from database)** read-only — tests use `fillKeysTabUserPin()` and click **List keys** without filling the read-only field. |

## Playwright embedded-live

| Rule | Detail |
| --- | --- |
| **Live API** | `PLAYWRIGHT_USE_LIVE_API = true` in `ui/e2e/constants.ts` on the lab host — no mocks for embedded-live specs. |
| **Admin token** | `DEV_ADMIN_TOKEN` in `constants.ts` (matches manifest `default_dev` / HKLM). |
| **Base URL** | `LAB_EMBEDDED_BASE_URL` → `https://192.168.55.197:8443`. |
| **No env shortcuts** | Do not use `$env:E2E_*` or `process.env` for lab config in committed e2e code — use `constants.ts` per `no-environment-variables.mdc`. |

## Lab provisioning sequence (after db-init)

```powershell
cd c:\analog-pim\pim-offline-server
cargo run --release --bin db-init -- --confirm --offline
cargo run --release --bin seed-dev -- --confirm --dev-fixtures --reset
pwsh .\scripts\Fix-LabSoftHsmLibraryPath.ps1
pwsh .\scripts\Prep-Beavis2LabCrypto.ps1 -ProvisionWrapKeys
Restart-Service aic-offline-server-service
# Required: prove endpoint + password recovery + elevation (or use -Repair)
pwsh .\scripts\Assert-Beavis2LabBaseline.ps1
```

Prefer one-shot restore: `pwsh .\scripts\Restore-Beavis2Lab.ps1` (see
`docs/dev/beavis2-lab-baseline.md`).

## Post-deploy baseline (mandatory)

Every build/deploy on this host must end with
`Assert-Beavis2LabBaseline.ps1` (hooked from `Deploy-OfflineServerDev.ps1`
when hostname/IP matches). If checks fail, restore before claiming done.
See always-apply rule `beavis2-lab-baseline-after-deploy.mdc`.

**Why it recurs:** `db-init` clears endpoints; deploy historically
restarted the service without `seed-dev` → zero machines, recover/elevation
broken.

## Password policy display format

Identity and reveal-password UI show rotation as **`DD:HH:MM:SS`** (not `Nd rotation`).
Embedded-live assertions MUST accept `\d+:\d{2}:\d{2}:\d{2} rotation` (seed-dev liebsoft uses `365:00:00:00`).
